  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">for support of expanding women&#x2019;s economic empowerment in Cameroon, Burkina Faso, and Tanzania</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As an African-headquartered research and capacity-strengthening organization, Partnership for Economic Policy (PEP) works with national research teams throughout the Global South to develop high-quality, locally generated evidence to inform better decisions in policy and practice. This grant will allow PEP to build on its emerging gendered economic analysis focal area to strengthen the capacities and influence of national research institutes in Burkina Faso, Cameroon, and Tanzania with demonstrated experience and motivation to engage with and inform gender-aware policymaking. 
(Strategy: International Women&apos;s Economic Empowerment)</narrative>
  </description>
